  "id": "perceptual-segregation",
  "term": "perceptual segregation",
  "definition": "Perceptual segregation is the process of separating overlapping sensory information into distinct sources, such as telling one talker’s audiovisual speech stream apart from another in a noisy social setting. In the supplied source, it is described as relying especially on audiovisual timing and on matching identity-related cues across face, voice, and language.",
